\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Calibri\" size=\"3\">In the example above for b1 each of the subjects had observations that\r\nmet the subset demands. </font></p><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;text-align:left;unicode-bidi:embed;direction:ltr\" dir=\"LTR\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Calibri\" size=\"3\">However, it can be that for a certain subject I won&#39;t have observations\r\nafter I subset. In this case I want to get NA in b2 for that subject in the\r\nspecific condition in which he doesn&#39;t have observations that meet the subset\r\ndemands. Does anyone have an idea for a way to do that?</font></p><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;text-align:left;unicode-bidi:embed;direction:ltr\" dir=\"LTR\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Calibri\" size=\"3\">Any help will be greatly appreciated.</font></p><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;text-align:left;unicode-bidi:embed;direction:ltr\" dir=\"LTR\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Calibri\" size=\"3\">Best,</font></p><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 10pt;text-align:left;unicode-bidi:embed;direction:ltr\" dir=\"LTR\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Calibri\" size=\"3\">Ayala</font></p><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font></div></div>"
